  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the tava or griddle to medium heat.",
    "In a large mortar and pestle, crush the blueberries until they release their juice.",
    "In a separate bowl, whisk together the almond flour, coconut sugar, eggs, flaxseed meal, salt, and vanilla extract.",
    "Gradually add the crushed blueberries to the dry mixture and mix until a dough forms.",
    "Add the warm water and mix until the dough comes together in a ball.",
    "Knead the dough for 2-3 minutes until it becomes smooth and elastic.",
    "Divide the dough into 2-3 equal pieces, depending on desired flatbread size.",
    "Roll out each piece into a thin circle, about 1/8 inch thick.",
    "Brush the flatbreads with olive oil and cook on the preheated tava or griddle for 2-3 minutes on each side.",
    "Serve warm and enjoy!",
    "Repeat with remaining dough pieces."
  ],
